      "content": "the 'fiscal oversight' thing sounds a bit thin though. the memo specifically shows he was against the *whole* thing, even the parts that aren't about money. if a reporter pushes back and asks, 'but he voted NO on the actual funding for the kids center, what's the real reason?', do we just tell them he changed his mind, or is there a better way to spin it so he doesn't look like he hates the community center?",
